3 December 1999		V1-0
	Current A&G.

22 December 1999        V1-1
        New routines to predict rotary table angles

10 March 2000           V3-0
        Health and CAR propagation changed (now with event processing)
        SNL changed, sequencer problems discovered/removed (delay function)
        Version is final version for software acceptance tests

31 March 2000           V3-1
	Applied counter torque ramp visualized in dm screen
	pimg made invisible and disabled (it is not to be used any more)

25 April 2000 until 05 May 2000		V3-2
	startup files changed (named N for North and S for South)
	parameter file (lut/pv) changes merged from Jena and Hawaii versions
	version number of PLC files jumped from V3.1 to V7.1 due to Hawaii 	
	  version system
	Probe arm PLC programs for PA3 and PA4 park further outside now.
	Chris Mayer's changes to capfast and c code implemented.
	Software ported from Epics Gem5 to Gem6 and Gem6T (Power PC)
	Put effort into avoiding warning messages from the strict PPC compiler
	"undefined" string created in look up table for all unknown positions
	"park-pos", "datum-pos" and "undefined" strings hidden from menus

25 October 2000        V3-4
        Orient the A&G x and y frame to the rest of the telescope. Do not
        use this release with versions of the TCS prior to V1-9.

04 February 2001       V4-0
        New accurate probe positioning code that removes the need for work
        rounds in the TCS plus a full simulation mode for testing new versions
        of the A&G off-line. Must be used with V2-0 or later of the TCS.
        Full details of the new features etc. can be found in ag_cjm_005.fm

05 May 2001            V4-1
        There is now only one set of calibration parameters for the probes and
        their subsystems rather than different sets depending on whether you
        consider individual mechanisms or the probe as one unit. The previous
        implementation could lead to the bizarre situation where a mechanism
        was apparently at two different places at the same time ! The new
        method removes this confusion and also means calibration parameters
        need only be specified once.

13 June 2001           V4-1-1
        Fix bug discovered by Roberto that loading the calibration display
        screens can give unconnected channels. The problem was using the
        incoorect display file in certain hierarchies.

17 June 2001           V4-2
        Reorganise and rename the LUT files. This was done to solve the 
        problem that the A&G always loaded the Gemini North files first. 
        For Gemini South this meant that often on a reboot all the LUT 
        tables had to be loaded by hand. Temporary work rounds were
        partially succesful but increased the boot time at Gemini South.
        Internally the CAD records are now named by new macros in 
        preparation for interfacing the hrwfs database to the OCS.

24 June 2001          V4-3
        HRWFS Mechanism CADs for Sel, Park and Datum renamed from
        hrwfs: to hrwfs:cc: This allows the new HRWFS software to 
        use the original names and thus preserve the OCS ICD. 

25 September 2001     V5-0
	Ported to EPICS 3.13.4GEM7. Tested on the hardware without the
	A&G Sequencer at the end of August.

05 October 2001       V5-1
        Updated LUT's and PV files with latest calibrations from Hilo and 
        La Serena. First operational version of A&G under 3.13 to
        coincide with release V3-1 of the A&G Sequencer.

04 December 2001      V5-2
        Important bug fix in ag_track.c that was setting the position and
        velocity demand to 0.0 for 0.2s whenever a new trackid was
        received. Also updated LUT's etc. with latest operational files
        and bash scripts to replace previous csh scripts.

13 December 2001      V5-3
        Implementation of the automatic sequencing of the optical encoders for
        the HRWFS Lens and Fieldstop mechanisms. In automatic mode, the encoders
        will be switched on before any command that moves the mechanism and off
        afterwards. In manual mode, the operator still needs to switch the
        encoders on before a move and off afterwards.

21 May 2002          V5-4
        Use dummy 4th coordinate to distinguish SF names that map to the 
        same x,y,z. Update the corresponding LUT files.

13 March 2003        V5-5
        Relatively minor changes to update lut and pv files and tidy code.
        Mainly built to coincide with release V3-4 of Sequencer and hence
        use GEM8.4

10 November 2003     V5-6
        Updates to get busy/idle working when following

21 November 2004     V5-7
	M304 and M1004 PMAC variables readout
	Code to keep small A&G Mechanism in position (like fieldstops)
	updated CP lut files and pv file.

02 December 2004     V5-8
        Added the following mech's p1_filter, p2_filter, clfilter and 
        ndfilter.

17 December 2004   (AWE: not V5-9 ... this was never tagged as a version
	I just noticed this after preparing and tagging V5-9 in April 2007.
	This must have been incorporated into V5-8 without a tag by Roberto??)
	Remove small bug in the algoritm to keep mech's in position.
	Added Reset Small Mechanism option to reset the amplifier
	Added a Dm-Screen to handle it

18 April 2007       V5-9  (AWE)
	Change In Position Logic for RT2.  It now holds position in closed loop
	and no longer requires the brakes to be on in order to report being In Position.

06 October 2009  V5-8-1 (PG)
	Branch from V5-8 (V5-8_F2AT1). The reason for having a branch is
	that V5-9 has been reported to have a bug and is not in use.
	V5-8-1 deals with the fact that Flamingos-2 lives on a separate
	subnet. The install script was modified to edit resource.def on
	the fly. Lookup table and pvload file were updated with the versions
	in use at the telescope.

24 January 2010  V5-8-2 (CUR)
	Added a new record (mbbip) with the same behaviour as mbbi,
	but with up to 24 values.

September, 2012  V5-10 (AWE)
	Merge the F2 branch back into trunk (the bug was removed in V5-9)
	Implement flexure compensation for PWFS1 and PWFS2.
	The compensation is initially off by default until the models are determined.
	Changes:
	capfast/ag/Makefile.Host
	capfast/ag/ccSysSub.sch
	capfast/ag/compCad.sch
	capfast/ag/pwfsSys.sch
	capfast/ag/simu_top.sch
	capfast/ag/specials.sch
	capfast/ag/tracking.sch
	capfast/ag/edb.def
	capfast/ag/embbip.sym
	capfast/ag/embbips.s
	src/CP/pv/gbd.pv
	src/CP/pv/pwfs1.pv
	src/CP/pv/pwfs2.pv
	src/MK/pv/pwfs1.pv
	src/MK/pv/pwfs2.pv
	src/ag/Makefile.Vx
	src/ag/ag_cad.c
	src/ag/ag_define.h
	src/ag/ag_gensub.c
	src/ag/ag_track.c
	src/ag/ag_utils.c
	src/ag/mbbipRecord.c
	src/ag/mbbipRecord.dbd
	src/ag/mbbipRecord.h
	startup/startup.vws
	startup/startupSim.vws
	(plus a merge of lut changes)

April, 2013  V5-11 (CUR)
        Added new SF positions in A&G for visitor instrumet (REL-788)
        src/MK/lut/ag_sf.lut
        src/CP/lut/ag_sf.lut

	Fixed calculation for probe rotary table and premature PWFS2 RT unwrap (REL-466)

April, 2013  V5-11-2 (CUR)

	REL-466 reversed. This still has some bugs.

August, 2013  V5-11-3 (CUR)

	Modified tracking algorithm.taking into consideration also the PA (REL-466)
	M src/CP/pv/pwfs2.pv
	M src/MK/pv/pwfs2.pv
	M src/ag/ag_utils.c

September, 2013 V5-11-4 (TCC)
	Added reading SF linear stage skew.

November, 2015 V5-11-5 (TCC)
	REL-2319: Added the GateWay EPICS database for multiple OI's.
